# Component API

Every component is CSS on semantic HTML. JavaScript, if any, only sets attributes.

## Class taxonomy (daisyUI-style)

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| component | `gx-<name>` | `gx-btn` |
| part | `gx-<name>-<part>` | `gx-panel-title`, `gx-textbox-speaker` |
| tone | `gx-<name>-<tone>` | `gx-btn-danger`, `gx-bar-hp` |
| size | `gx-<name>-{sm,lg}` | `gx-btn-lg` |
| modifier | `gx-<name>-<modifier>` | `gx-bar-critical`, `gx-panel-flat` |

Tones are `primary`, `danger`, `success`, `warning`, `ghost`; messages (alert, toast) use
`info` for the primary tone. Game tones where they mean something: `hp`, `mp`, `xp`, and the
shared rarity modifier `gx-rarity-{common,rare,epic,legendary}` that cards and slots read via
`--gx-rarity`. Use the same names across components.

## State comes from the DOM, not extra classes

- Pressed: `:active`, `aria-pressed="true"`, `[data-pressed]`.
- Disabled: `:disabled`, `aria-disabled="true"`.
- Values: custom properties on the element (`style="--gx-value: 0.6"`) mirrored by ARIA
  (`aria-valuenow`). Open: native `[open]`.

## Structure of a component file

1. Component custom properties first (`--gx-btn-bg`), derived colours via `color-mix()`.
2. Base rule, then hover (inside `@media (hover: hover)`), `:focus-visible`, pressed,
   disabled, tones, sizes.
3. Raised parts reserve their own footprint with margin (`--gx-px` around,
   `--gx-px + --gx-depth` below) so pixel frames and depth never overlap neighbours.

## Definition of done

Component CSS in `components/`, imported by `index.css`, shown in `demo/` in every tone and
state, added to the `check-css.mjs` selector list, README table row, CHANGELOG entry.
